WEBVTT

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.420
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off --

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:32.520
Saving people, hunting things.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:33.690
The family business.

00:10:35.379 --> 00:10:37.270
Anybody here?

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.250
Dont move.

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:42.470
Sam? Dean?

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:43.610
Mom, you know these guys?

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:45.810
I think these are
John Winchesters boys.

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.830
Hey, Im Ellen. That's my daughter, Jo.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.200
You're not gonna hit me again, are you?

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:50.980
You called our dad, said you could help.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:51.730
Help with what?

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:53.110
The demon, of course.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:54.550
How do you know about all this?

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.170
Hey, I just run a saloon.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:58.530
Hunters have been known to
pass through now and again --

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:01.870
Including your dada long time
ago. John was like family once.

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:03.720
You think dad and
Ellen never had a thing?

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:04.850
No way.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.780
Then why didn't he tell us about her?

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.890
How did your mom get into this stuff?

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:13.120
My dad. He was a hunter. He passed away.

00:11:13.379 --> 00:11:13.980
I could help

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.830
I'm sure you could, but I
think your mother might kill me.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:18.759
You're afraid of my mother?

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:20.400
I think so.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:42.640
I checked the fuses. They're fine.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.390
It's the wiring!

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:48.250
Look, you promised this place
would be ready when I moved in.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.590
No! You come up now!

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:53.790
Please.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:56.060
Thank you.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.050
Gross.

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:45.779
What the hell?

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:12.710
Los Angeles, California.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:14.290
What's in L.A.?

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:16.730
A young girl's been
kidnapped by an evil cult.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:17.920
Yeah?

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.300
The girl got a name? Katie Holmes.

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:26.460
That's funny.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:33.230
Of course, on the other hand, catfight.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:35.170
I am your mother! I don't
have to be reasonable!

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:36.880
You can't keep me here!

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:38.100
Don't you bet on that, sweetie!

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.130
Are you gonna chain
me up in the basement?

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.410
You've had worse ideas
than that recently.

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:44.470
You don't want to stay?
Don't -Go back to school!

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:47.290
I didn't belong there! I was a
freak with a knife collection!

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:50.529
Getting yourself killed on some dusty
back road -That's where you belong?

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:57.890
Guys, bad time. Yes, ma'am.

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:00.130
We rarely drink before 10:00 anyway.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:01.450
Wait.

00:14:02.279 --> 00:14:03.800
I want to know what
they think about this.

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:05.820
I don't care what they think!

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.279
Are you guys open?

00:14:07.279 --> 00:14:08.800
Yes! No!

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:15.410
We'll just check out
the Arby's down the road.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:37.519
Harvelle's.

00:14:37.519 --> 00:14:39.450
Yeah, preacher.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:42.490
Three weeks ago, a young girl
disappears from a Philadelphia apartment.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:46.019
Take it. It won't bite.

00:14:46.019 --> 00:14:48.450
No, but your mom might.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:55.300
And this girl wasn't the first. Over the
past 80 years,6 women have vanished --

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:57.840
All from the same
building, all young blondes.

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:00.430
It only happens every decade or two,
so cops never eyeball the pattern.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:03.769
So we're either dealing with
one very old serial killer --

00:15:03.769 --> 00:15:06.730
Who put this together? Ash?

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:08.410
I did it myself.

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:14.300
I got to admit, we hit
the road for a lot less.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:16.390
Good. If you like the
case so much, you take it.

00:15:16.769 --> 00:15:19.750
Joanna Beth, this
family has lost enough.

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.720
I won't lose you, too.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.830
I just wont.

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:31.519
Mother told me

00:15:31.519 --> 00:15:33.720
Yes, she told me

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:36.980
I'd meet girls like you

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:38.800
She also told me,

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:40.789
"Stay away

00:15:40.789 --> 00:15:44.310
You'll never know what you'll catch"

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:46.180
Mommy's all right,

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:47.650
Daddys all right,

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:51.130
They just seem a little weird.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:54.710
Surrender, surrender.

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.500
I feel kind of bad, snaking jobs case.

00:15:59.769 --> 00:16:02.509
Well, maybe she put
together a good file,

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:05.720
But could you see her out here
working one of these things?

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:07.590
I don't think so.

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:10.830
You getting anything?

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.830
No, not yet.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:20.570
What's that?

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.420
What?

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:29.550
Holy crap.

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:39.009
That's ectoplasm.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:41.950
Well, Sam, I think I know
what we're dealing with here.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.720
It's the stay-Puft marshmallow man.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:50.330
Dean, Ive only seen
this stuff like twice.

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:53.970
I mean, to make this stuff, you have
to be one majorly pissed-Off spirit.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.700
Let's find this badass before
he snags any more girls.

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:04.140
Yeah, it's a great building.
I fixed it up real nice.

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:05.529
All the apartments come furnished, too.

00:17:05.529 --> 00:17:09.300
Yeah, I love the
furnishings. It's so spacious,

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:13.640
And the location is
so convenient for me.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.289
What the hell are you doing here?

00:17:15.289 --> 00:17:17.150
There you are, honey.

00:17:18.759 --> 00:17:21.160
This is my boyfriend,
Dean, and his buddy Sam.

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.930
Good to meet you. Quite
a gal you got here.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:25.840
Yeah, she's a pistol!

00:17:26.009 --> 00:17:28.539
So, did you already
check out the apartment?

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:32.180
The one for rent.

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:35.470
Yeah. Yes. Loved it. Great flow.

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:37.140
How'd you get in? It was open.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:40.890
Now, Ed, when did the
last tenant move out?

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.090
Uh, about a month ago. Cut and run, too.

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:45.099
Stiffed me for the rent.

00:17:45.099 --> 00:17:47.870
Well, her loss, our gain,

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:50.210
'Cause if Dean loves it,
it's good enough for me.

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:52.160
Oh, sweetie.

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:54.509
We'll take it.

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:58.450
Okay.

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:03.240
I'll flip you for the sofa.

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:04.599
Does your mother even know youre here?

00:18:04.599 --> 00:18:05.809
I told her I was going to Vegas.

00:18:05.809 --> 00:18:06.900
You think shes gonna buy that?

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:07.779
I'm not an idiot.

00:18:07.779 --> 00:18:10.710
I got Ash to lay a credit-Card
trail all the way to the casinos.

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:15.110
You shouldn't lie to your mom.
You shouldn't be here, either.

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:20.160
Well, I am, so untwist your
boxers and deal with it.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.099
Where'd you get all
that money from, anyways?

00:18:22.099 --> 00:18:23.099
Working at the roadhouse.

00:18:23.099 --> 00:18:24.340
Hunters don't tip that well.

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:26.340
They aren't that good at poker, either.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:34.620
Yeah? Is she with you?

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:36.809
Oh, hi, Ellen.

00:18:36.809 --> 00:18:39.450
She left a note shes in Vegas.
I don't believe it for a second.

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:44.039
Dean? I haven't seen her.

00:18:44.039 --> 00:18:46.300
You sure about that? Yeah, Im sure.

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:49.430
Well, please, if she shows up, you'll
drag her butt back here, won't you?

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:51.539
Absolutely. Okay. Thanks, hon.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:58.519
This place was built in 1924.

00:18:58.519 --> 00:19:01.880
It was originally a warehouse, converted
into apartments a few months ago.

00:19:02.789 --> 00:19:05.210
Yeah? What was here before 1924?

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:06.590
Nothing. An empty field.

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:08.470
So the most
likely scenario --

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:11.740
Someone died bloody in the building,
and now he's back and raising hell.

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:14.750
I already checked.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:17.450
In the past 82 years,
zero violent deaths,

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:19.780
Unless you count a janitor
who slipped on a wet floor.

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:22.610
Would you sit down, please?

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:28.490
So, have you checked the police
reports, county death records?

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:31.990
Obituaries, mortuary reports,
and seven other sources.

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:33.059
I know what I'm doing.

00:19:33.059 --> 00:19:35.240
I think the jury's
still out on that one.

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:39.769
Would you put the knife down?

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.410
Okay. So, uh, its something else, then.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.050
Maybe some kind of cursed object
that brought a spirit with it.

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:48.880
We got to scan the whole
building. Right. So, you and me --

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:52.559
Well take the top two floors.

00:19:52.559 --> 00:19:54.780
We'd move faster if we split up.

00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:56.680
Oh, this isn't negotiable.

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:00.680
So, are you gonna buy me dinner?

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:02.930
What are you talking about?

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:06.730
It's just if you're gonna ride me this
close, it's only decent you buy me dinner.

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:08.680
Oh, that's hilarious.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:10.220
Its bad enough I lied to your mom,

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:12.180
But if you think I'm letting
you out of my sight --

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:14.660
I don't know if you noticed, but
you're kind of the spirit's type.

00:20:15.039 --> 00:20:16.380
Exactly.

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:18.599
You want to be bait?

00:20:18.599 --> 00:20:20.440
The quickest way to draw
it out, and you know it.

00:20:21.039 --> 00:20:22.590
What? I'm so regretting this.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:25.710
I've had it up to herewith your crap.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:27.400
Excuse me?

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:29.099
Your chauvinist crap.

00:20:29.099 --> 00:20:30.769
You think women cant do the job.

00:20:30.769 --> 00:20:34.320
Sweetheart, this ain't gender
studies. Women can do the job fine.

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:36.700
Amateurs cant. You got no experience.

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:41.320
What you do have is a bunch of half-Baked romantic
notions that some barfly has put in your head.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:42.960
And now you sound like my mother.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:45.170
Oh, and that's a bad thing?
Because let me tell you --

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:47.110
What?

00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:51.039
Forget it.

00:20:51.039 --> 00:20:52.490
No, you started this.

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:56.210
Jo, you got options. No one in
their right mind chooses this life.

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:59.579
My dad started me in this when I was so
young. I wish I could do something else.

00:20:59.579 --> 00:21:00.809
You love the job.

00:21:00.809 --> 00:21:02.250
Yeah, but Im a little twisted.

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:04.890
You don't think Im
a little twisted, too?

00:21:06.539 --> 00:21:08.829
Jo, you got a mother
that worries about you,

00:21:08.829 --> 00:21:12.160
Who wants something more for
you. Those are good things.

00:21:12.820 --> 00:21:15.539
You don't throw things like that away.

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:18.259
They might be hard to find later.

00:21:55.619 --> 00:21:56.990
What?

00:21:59.780 --> 00:22:01.450
I'm not sure.

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:05.610
Do you smell that?

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:09.059
What is it, a gas leak?

00:22:09.059 --> 00:22:11.420
No. Its something else.

00:22:13.059 --> 00:22:16.890
I know it. I just can't
put my finger on it.

00:22:23.880 --> 00:22:26.220
Mazel Tov. You just
found your first spirit.

00:22:27.440 --> 00:22:29.460
It's inside the vent.

00:22:36.090 --> 00:22:37.670
Here.

00:22:57.519 --> 00:22:59.160
There's something in there. Here.

00:23:21.829 --> 00:23:24.140
Someone's keeping souvenirs.

00:24:16.269 --> 00:24:18.530
This building --
I swear to god.

00:24:42.730 --> 00:24:44.610
I'm so out of here.

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:28.680
Morning, princess.

00:25:29.470 --> 00:25:31.740
Where's Sam? Went to get coffee.

00:25:36.730 --> 00:25:38.430
My back.

00:25:40.920 --> 00:25:43.809
How'd you sleep on that big, soft bed?

00:25:43.809 --> 00:25:45.460
I didnt.

00:25:45.460 --> 00:25:48.000
I've just been going over everything.

00:26:00.920 --> 00:26:02.530
Here.

00:26:02.530 --> 00:26:03.860
What's this for?

00:26:03.860 --> 00:26:07.269
It'll work a hell of a lot better than that
little pig stick you've been twirling around.

00:26:20.530 --> 00:26:23.160
William Anthony Harvelle.

00:26:25.579 --> 00:26:27.980
I'm sorry. My mistake.

00:26:38.720 --> 00:26:40.860
What do
you --

00:26:40.860 --> 00:26:42.849
What do you remember about your dad?

00:26:43.590 --> 00:26:46.550
What's the first thing
that pops into your head?

00:26:51.079 --> 00:26:53.360
Come on. Tell me.

00:27:01.190 --> 00:27:03.769
I was 6 or 7...

00:27:04.849 --> 00:27:07.019
And, uh...

00:27:07.559 --> 00:27:09.990
He took me shooting for the first time.

00:27:09.990 --> 00:27:13.039
Bottles on a fence
--That kind of thing.

00:27:14.349 --> 00:27:16.490
I bull's-Eyed every one of them.

00:27:18.450 --> 00:27:21.730
And he would smile, like...

00:27:24.720 --> 00:27:26.440
I dont know.

00:27:28.650 --> 00:27:30.660
He must have been proud.

00:27:33.299 --> 00:27:35.590
What about your dad?

00:27:37.620 --> 00:27:40.460
I was still in pigtails
when my dad died, but...

00:27:41.380 --> 00:27:44.340
I remember him coming home from a hunt.

00:27:44.819 --> 00:27:47.210
He'd burst through
that door like --

00:27:47.410 --> 00:27:49.930
Like Steve McQueen or something.

00:27:50.799 --> 00:27:53.110
And he'd sweep me up in his arms,

00:27:53.480 --> 00:27:56.049
And I'd breathe in that
old leather jacket of his.

00:27:57.539 --> 00:28:00.700
And my mom --Who
was sour and pissed

00:28:00.700 --> 00:28:03.750
From the minute he left
She started smiling again.

00:28:04.789 --> 00:28:06.650
And we were...

00:28:07.910 --> 00:28:09.789
We were a family.

00:28:16.190 --> 00:28:18.789
You want to know why
I want to do the job?

00:28:19.630 --> 00:28:21.819
For him.

00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:24.910
It's my way of being close to him.

00:28:26.059 --> 00:28:28.190
Now, tell me, what's wrong with that?

00:28:29.789 --> 00:28:31.559
Nothing.

00:28:37.960 --> 00:28:40.289
Where's the coffee?
There are cops outside.

00:28:41.269 --> 00:28:43.390
Another girl disappeared.

00:28:51.450 --> 00:28:54.000
Theresa Ellis
--Apartment 2-F.

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:56.230
Her boyfriend reported
her missing around dawn.

00:28:56.230 --> 00:28:57.769
And her apartment?

00:28:57.769 --> 00:29:00.700
Cracks all over the
plaster --Walls, ceiling.

00:29:00.700 --> 00:29:02.210
There's ectoplasm, too.

00:29:02.210 --> 00:29:05.410
Between that and that tuft of hair, I'd
say the suckers coming from the walls.

00:29:05.410 --> 00:29:08.670
But who is it? The building's
history's totally clean.

00:29:11.069 --> 00:29:13.289
Maybe we're looking in the wrong place.

00:29:13.289 --> 00:29:15.870
What do you mean? Check this out.

00:29:19.529 --> 00:29:20.680
An empty field?

00:29:20.680 --> 00:29:24.470
It's where this building was built.
Take a look at the one next door.

00:29:25.830 --> 00:29:28.250
The windows.

00:29:30.190 --> 00:29:31.220
Bars.

00:29:31.220 --> 00:29:33.130
We're next door to a prison?

00:29:33.130 --> 00:29:34.380
Thanks, Ash.

00:29:34.380 --> 00:29:36.410
Oh, and if you breathe a
word of this to my mom --

00:29:36.410 --> 00:29:40.460
Thats right. I will. With pliers.

00:29:41.120 --> 00:29:43.450
Okay. Moyamensing
prison --

00:29:43.450 --> 00:29:47.230
Built in 1835, torn down
in 1963. And get this --

00:29:47.230 --> 00:29:51.080
They used to execute people by hanging
them in the empty field next door.

00:29:52.330 --> 00:29:55.590
Well, then, we need a list of
all the people executed there.

00:29:55.590 --> 00:29:57.559
Ash is already on it.

00:30:03.940 --> 00:30:06.630
157 names?

00:30:07.069 --> 00:30:09.110
We got to narrow that down. Yeah.

00:30:09.110 --> 00:30:11.789
Or else we're gonna be digging
up a hell of a lot of stiffs.

00:30:18.930 --> 00:30:20.900
Herman Webster Mudgett?

00:30:22.529 --> 00:30:24.279
Yeah?

00:30:25.250 --> 00:30:28.259
Wasn't that H.H. Holmes' real name?

00:30:29.769 --> 00:30:32.180
You got to be kidding me.

00:30:38.559 --> 00:30:41.940
Holmes was executed at
Moyamensing may 7,1896.

00:30:42.029 --> 00:30:44.190
H.H. Holmes himself.

00:30:44.600 --> 00:30:46.340
Come on. I mean, what are the odds?

00:30:46.340 --> 00:30:48.170
Who is this guy?

00:30:48.170 --> 00:30:51.500
The term "multi-Murderer" --
They coined it to describe Holmes.

00:30:51.500 --> 00:30:54.799
He was Americas first serial killer before
anybody knew what a serial killer was.

00:30:54.799 --> 00:30:58.319
He confessed to 27 murders, but
some put the death toll at over 100.

00:30:58.319 --> 00:31:01.920
And his victim flavor of
choice -Pretty, petite blondes.

00:31:02.319 --> 00:31:05.319
He, uh, used chloroform to kill them,

00:31:06.250 --> 00:31:08.620
Which is what I smelled
in the hallway last night.

00:31:10.750 --> 00:31:12.480
At his place, cops found human remains,

00:31:12.480 --> 00:31:16.100
Bone fragments, and long
locks of bloody blond hair.

00:31:16.100 --> 00:31:18.220
Boy, he sure knew how to pick them.

00:31:18.220 --> 00:31:20.890
We just find the bones, salt
them, and burn them, right?

00:31:20.890 --> 00:31:22.220
It's not that easy.

00:31:22.220 --> 00:31:24.500
His body is buried in town,

00:31:24.500 --> 00:31:27.200
But it's encased in a
couple tons of concrete.

00:31:27.200 --> 00:31:28.910
What? Why?

00:31:28.910 --> 00:31:32.190
The story goes that he didn't
want anybody mutilating his corpse

00:31:32.190 --> 00:31:34.910
'Cause, you know, it's
what he used to do.

00:31:34.910 --> 00:31:36.819
You know something?

00:31:38.940 --> 00:31:40.799
We might have an even
bigger problem than that.

00:31:40.799 --> 00:31:42.779
How does this get bigger?

00:31:43.480 --> 00:31:45.740
Holmes built an apartment
building in Chicago.

00:31:45.740 --> 00:31:49.039
They called it the murder castle.
The whole place was a death factory.

00:31:49.039 --> 00:31:52.200
They had trapdoors, acid
vats, quicklime pits.

00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:54.809
He built these secret chambers...

00:31:54.809 --> 00:31:56.720
Inside the walls.

00:31:56.720 --> 00:31:58.930
He'd lock his victims in,
keep them alive for days.

00:31:58.930 --> 00:32:00.730
Some, he'd suffocate.

00:32:00.730 --> 00:32:02.860
Others, he'd let starve to death.

00:32:02.860 --> 00:32:06.900
So Theresa could still be alive.
She could be inside these walls.

00:32:06.900 --> 00:32:09.360
We need sledgehammers, crowbars.
We got to smash these walls

00:32:09.360 --> 00:32:11.620
Anywhere thick enough to hide a girl.

00:32:26.309 --> 00:32:29.700
Okay. Call us after you
check the southeast wall.

00:32:30.809 --> 00:32:33.630
Sam's almost done with the first floor.

00:32:34.100 --> 00:32:36.330
He hasn't found jack squat, either.

00:32:43.110 --> 00:32:44.350
What is it?

00:32:44.350 --> 00:32:46.900
It's too narrow. We
can't go any further.

00:32:46.900 --> 00:32:48.600
Let me see. -
What are you --

00:32:52.110 --> 00:32:54.009
I should have cleaned the pipes. What?

00:32:54.009 --> 00:32:56.460
I wish the pipes were clean.

00:32:56.990 --> 00:32:58.430
Shut up!

00:32:58.430 --> 00:32:59.950
I can fit in there.

00:33:00.340 --> 00:33:01.700
You're not going in thereby yourself.

00:33:01.700 --> 00:33:03.309
You got a better idea?

00:33:03.309 --> 00:33:04.740
The
--

00:33:27.980 --> 00:33:30.200
Where are you? By the north wall.

00:33:50.210 --> 00:33:53.140
I'm heading down some kind of air duct.

00:33:53.140 --> 00:33:54.970
No, no, no, no. Stay up here.

00:33:54.970 --> 00:33:57.100
We got to find this girl, don't we?

00:33:57.740 --> 00:33:59.170
I'm okay.

00:33:59.170 --> 00:34:01.110
All right. Im heading to you.

00:34:35.590 --> 00:34:36.909
Oh, god.

00:34:37.539 --> 00:34:39.110
What is it?

00:34:40.010 --> 00:34:42.489
Jo? Jo?!

00:34:50.720 --> 00:34:52.119
Jo!

00:35:14.069 --> 00:35:15.840
Jo?!

00:35:18.210 --> 00:35:19.960
Jo!

00:35:29.199 --> 00:35:31.319
He's got Jo. What? Howd that happen?

00:35:31.319 --> 00:35:33.390
I wasn't with her. I
left her alone. Damn it!

00:35:33.390 --> 00:35:36.190
Look, we'll find her. Where? Inside
the walls. We were inside the walls.

00:35:36.190 --> 00:35:39.529
None of the other girls are
there. She won't be, either.

00:35:40.539 --> 00:35:43.350
Look, take a beat and think about
this. Maybe we got Holmes' M.O. Wrong.

00:35:43.350 --> 00:35:45.369
Well, we better friggin' think fast.

00:35:48.909 --> 00:35:49.800
Yeah?

00:35:49.800 --> 00:35:51.769
You lied to me. Shes there.

00:35:51.769 --> 00:35:54.079
Ellen. Ash told me everything.

00:35:54.079 --> 00:35:56.100
The man's a genius, but
he folds like a cheap suit.

00:35:56.100 --> 00:35:57.579
You put my damn daughter on the phone.

00:35:57.579 --> 00:36:01.000
She's gonna have to call you back. She's,
uh, taking care of feminine business.

00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:03.220
Yeah, right. Where is she?

00:36:03.690 --> 00:36:05.680
Where is she?!

00:36:06.119 --> 00:36:07.279
Look, we'll get her back.

00:36:07.279 --> 00:36:09.720
Get her back? Back from what?

00:36:09.720 --> 00:36:11.390
The spirit we're
hunting --It took her.

00:36:11.390 --> 00:36:12.110
Oh, my god.

00:36:12.110 --> 00:36:13.630
She'll be okay. I promise. You promise?

00:36:13.630 --> 00:36:17.500
That is not the first time Ive
heard that from a Winchester.

00:36:17.750 --> 00:36:18.619
What?

00:36:18.619 --> 00:36:20.539
If anything
happens to her --

00:36:20.539 --> 00:36:22.069
It wont. I won't let it.

00:36:22.069 --> 00:36:23.880
Ellen, Im sorry. I really am.

00:36:23.880 --> 00:36:26.569
I'm taking the first flight out.
I'll be there in a few hours.

00:36:29.029 --> 00:36:31.319
Damn it!

00:36:31.319 --> 00:36:34.380
Don't beat yourself up, Dean.
There's nothing you could have done.

00:36:34.380 --> 00:36:35.890
Tell me you got something.

00:36:35.890 --> 00:36:37.159
Uh, maybe.

00:36:38.600 --> 00:36:39.880
Look.

00:36:39.880 --> 00:36:41.650
If you look at the layout
of the Holmes murder castle,

00:36:41.650 --> 00:36:43.920
Theres other torture chambers
inside the walls, right?

00:36:44.340 --> 00:36:46.329
But there's one we
havent considered yet --

00:36:46.329 --> 00:36:47.690
The one in his basement.

00:36:47.690 --> 00:36:48.750
This building doesn't have a basement.

00:36:48.750 --> 00:36:51.409
You're right. It doesnt.
But I just noticed this.

00:36:51.500 --> 00:36:53.019
Beneath the foundation,

00:36:53.019 --> 00:36:55.230
It looks like part of an old sewer
system. It hasn't been used for --

00:36:55.230 --> 00:36:56.680
Lets go.

00:38:07.279 --> 00:38:08.610
Hello?

00:38:18.619 --> 00:38:20.600
Is -Is anybody there?

00:38:21.230 --> 00:38:23.610
Your name's Theresa?

00:38:25.019 --> 00:38:26.699
Yes.

00:38:26.699 --> 00:38:29.550
This won't make you feel better, but...

00:38:30.119 --> 00:38:32.329
I'm here to rescue you.

00:38:32.960 --> 00:38:36.119
Oh, god. He's out there.
He's gonna kill us!

00:38:36.119 --> 00:38:38.190
No, he won't!

00:38:38.190 --> 00:38:40.460
We're getting out.

00:38:40.460 --> 00:38:43.170
My friends are looking for us.

00:38:44.059 --> 00:38:45.920
Oh, god, it's him!

00:38:45.920 --> 00:38:48.230
Shh! Just be quiet!

00:39:49.840 --> 00:39:51.460
Here.

00:40:18.519 --> 00:40:20.190
Got it? Yeah.

00:41:22.250 --> 00:41:23.890
You're so pretty.

00:41:28.010 --> 00:41:29.920
So beautiful.

00:41:29.920 --> 00:41:31.940
Go to hell!

00:42:04.880 --> 00:42:06.500
How do you like that?!

00:42:06.500 --> 00:42:09.489
Pure iron, you
creepy-Ass son of a bitch!

00:43:12.970 --> 00:43:14.800
Is he gone?

00:43:15.869 --> 00:43:17.869
I don't
know. I --

00:43:35.730 --> 00:43:37.369
Hey!

00:43:38.420 --> 00:43:39.769
No!

00:43:41.329 --> 00:43:42.569
Jo!

00:43:42.989 --> 00:43:44.739
I'm here!

00:44:09.159 --> 00:44:11.079
Hey. I'm gonna get you
out of here, all right?

00:44:11.610 --> 00:44:13.260
Sam!

00:44:15.569 --> 00:44:17.269
Hang on.

00:44:20.140 --> 00:44:22.750
You all right? I've been better.

00:44:23.300 --> 00:44:25.899
Let's get the hell out of
here before he comes back.

00:44:25.899 --> 00:44:28.939
Actually, I don't think
you're leaving here just yet.

00:44:28.939 --> 00:44:29.619
What?

00:44:29.619 --> 00:44:32.199
Remember when I said you
being bait was a bad plan?

00:44:32.199 --> 00:44:34.350
Now it's kind of the only one we got.

00:45:49.300 --> 00:45:50.619
Now!

00:46:10.220 --> 00:46:14.149
Scream all you want! There's no
way you're stepping over that salt!

00:46:24.699 --> 00:46:26.359
So...

00:46:26.359 --> 00:46:29.069
Is this job as glamorous
as you thought it would be?

00:46:30.090 --> 00:46:32.480
Well, except for all the
peeYour-Pants terror, yeah.

00:46:33.140 --> 00:46:35.899
But that Theresa girl's gonna
live a life 'cause of us.

00:46:36.270 --> 00:46:37.560
It's worth it, isn't it?

00:46:37.560 --> 00:46:38.989
Yeah.

00:46:38.989 --> 00:46:40.439
Yeah, it is.

00:46:40.439 --> 00:46:42.380
Hey, what if somebody
finds that sewer done there

00:46:42.380 --> 00:46:44.279
Or a storm washes the salt away?

00:46:44.279 --> 00:46:47.600
Both very fine points, which
is why we're waiting here.

00:46:47.600 --> 00:46:49.109
For what?

00:46:55.529 --> 00:46:57.170
For that.

00:47:18.409 --> 00:47:20.350
You ripped off a cement truck?

00:47:20.350 --> 00:47:21.859
I'll give it back.

00:47:37.300 --> 00:47:40.439
Well, that ought to keep him
down there till hell freezes over.

00:48:14.039 --> 00:48:17.539
Well, you -You really weren't
kidding about flying out, were you?

00:48:30.869 --> 00:48:32.939
How about we listen to some music?

00:48:33.680 --> 00:48:36.730
You're as cold as ice.

00:48:47.340 --> 00:48:49.550
This is gonna be a long drive.

00:48:57.239 --> 00:48:59.000
Ellen...

00:48:59.000 --> 00:49:02.859
It was my fault. Okay? I
lied to you, and I'm sorry.

00:49:02.859 --> 00:49:05.119
But Jo did good out there. I
think her dad would be proud.

00:49:05.119 --> 00:49:07.800
Don't you dare
say that --Not you.

00:49:07.800 --> 00:49:10.430
I need a moment with
my daughter -Alone.

00:49:19.470 --> 00:49:21.020
You're angry. I understand.

00:49:21.020 --> 00:49:22.909
Angry doesn't beg into touch it!

00:49:22.909 --> 00:49:25.560
Let's just think about
this. Everything's okay.

00:49:25.560 --> 00:49:27.050
I'm alive.

00:49:27.050 --> 00:49:28.590
Not after Im through with you!

00:49:28.590 --> 00:49:30.020
Is this about me hunting
or something else?

00:49:30.020 --> 00:49:31.640
You let those boys use you as bait.

00:49:31.640 --> 00:49:33.409
They were backing me up the whole time.

00:49:33.409 --> 00:49:35.319
That is why you do not have
the sense to do this job.

00:49:35.319 --> 00:49:37.060
You're trusting your life to
them. What are you talking about?

00:49:37.060 --> 00:49:39.420
Like father, like son.
That is what Im talking...

00:49:44.720 --> 00:49:46.470
John?

00:49:49.000 --> 00:49:51.199
I thought you and John were friends.

00:49:51.199 --> 00:49:53.319
Yeah, we were. I'm
sorry. I didn't mean --

00:49:53.319 --> 00:49:54.730
Mom...

00:49:57.420 --> 00:50:00.000
What aren't you telling me?

00:50:16.210 --> 00:50:18.069
That bad, huh? Not right now.

00:50:19.670 --> 00:50:21.340
What happened? Hey, talk to me.

00:50:21.340 --> 00:50:23.010
Get off me!

00:50:23.590 --> 00:50:25.390
Sorry. Ill see you around.

00:50:25.390 --> 00:50:27.600
Dean...

00:50:31.430 --> 00:50:34.529
It turns out my dad had a
partner on his last hunt.

00:50:34.529 --> 00:50:36.810
Funny, he usually worked
alone. This guy did, too.

00:50:36.810 --> 00:50:40.810
But I guess my father
figured he could trust him.

00:50:41.569 --> 00:50:45.260
A mistake. The guy screwed
up, got my dad killed.

00:50:45.260 --> 00:50:47.619
What does this have --
It was your father, Dean.

00:50:48.640 --> 00:50:50.180
What?

00:50:50.180 --> 00:50:53.789
Why do you think John never came
back, never told you about us?

00:50:53.789 --> 00:50:56.689
'Cause he couldn't look my mom
in the eye after that -That's why.

00:50:57.130 --> 00:50:58.829
Jo --
Just --

00:50:58.829 --> 00:51:01.060
Just get out of here.

00:51:01.899 --> 00:51:03.739
Please, just leave.



00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.700
